# Supabase RLS and tenant isolation

## Non-negotiables

- Never weaken Row Level Security policies or bypass RLS with service-role keys in user-facing paths.
- Preserve tenant isolation: every query must scope by organization/tenant as the existing code does.
- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` or other secrets to client bundles or logs.

## Schema changes

- All schema changes require a new migration in `supabase/migrations/`.
- New tables with tenant data MUST enable RLS and include policies consistent with existing patterns.
- Security-sensitive policy changes require explicit human review before merge.

## Development safety

- Do not modify production Supabase data during development.
- Prefer local Supabase (`supabase start`) or isolated test projects for destructive tests.
- Read-only verification scripts are preferred for live schema checks.

## Review checklist

- [ ] RLS enabled on new/changed tables
- [ ] Policies tested for cross-tenant denial
- [ ] Server routes use appropriate client (user session vs service role)
- [ ] Migration is reversible or rollback documented in plan
